---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const launchCheckoutUrl = 'https://buy.stripe.com/eVq8wPaNo7k71gVb2U57W03';
---

<Base title="Chauncy Pricing" description="Buy Chauncy for Windows at the $99 early adopter launch price. Regular pricing is planned at $149 after the launch allocation.">

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container launch-container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Windows launch price available now</p>
      <h1>Buy Chauncy once. Keep your archive local.</h1>
      <p class="page-sub">
        The early adopter Windows license is available for $99. After the first launch allocation, regular one-time pricing is planned at $149.
      </p>

      <div class="launch-grid">
        <div class="launch-card highlighted">
          <span class="badge">Planned launch price</span>
          <h2>$99</h2>
          <p>First 100 licenses during the Windows launch.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Chauncy for Windows at launch</li>
            <li>Linux build when verified for release</li>
            <li>macOS build included when released</li>
            <li>All current features</li>
            <li>14-day money-back guarantee</li>
          </ul>
          <a href={launchCheckoutUrl} class="btn btn-primary card-cta">Buy Chauncy - $99</a>
        </div>
        <div class="launch-card">
          <span class="badge muted">Regular price</span>
          <h2>$149</h2>
          <p>Standard one-time license after the launch allocation is gone.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>No subscription</li>
            <li>No Chauncy cloud account</li>
            <li>No telemetry</li>
            <li>Bring your own AI provider or local endpoint</li>
            <li>Your archive stays on your machine</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="fine-print">Secure checkout is handled by Stripe. After payment, Stripe redirects to the Chauncy download page.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-alt">
    <div class="container readiness">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Purchase flow</p>
        <h2>What happens after checkout.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="readiness-list">
        <div>
          <h3>Stripe checkout</h3>
          <p>Payment is processed by Stripe using the $99 launch Payment Link.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Download delivery</h3>
          <p>After payment, Stripe redirects to the Chauncy download page with the Windows installer and SHA-256 checksum.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Local-first use</h3>
          <p>Chauncy runs on your computer. Your archive, search index, and annotations stay local.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container faq-on-pricing">
      <h2>Common questions</h2>

      <details>
        <summary>Is Chauncy still a one-time purchase?</summary>
        <p>Yes. Buy once and use Chauncy without a subscription.</p>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>What happens after I pay?</summary>
        <p>Stripe redirects you to the Chauncy download page for the Windows installer. Your receipt is handled by Stripe.</p>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>Is the $99 price permanent?</summary>
        <p>No. The $99 price is the early adopter Windows launch price for the first 100 licenses. Regular pricing is planned at $149.</p>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>Will privacy claims change when sales open?</summary>
        <p>No. Chauncy remains local-first, account-free, telemetry-free, and explicit about any optional AI provider request.</p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </section>

</Base>

<style>
  .launch-container {
    max-width: 900px;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .launch-container h1 {
    margin: 0.8rem auto 0;
    max-width: 820px;
    font-size: clamp(2.1rem, 5vw, 4rem);
  }

  .page-sub {
    margin: 1rem auto 2.5rem;
    max-width: 720px;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: 1.12rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  .launch-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: 1.25rem;
    margin: 0 auto 1.5rem;
    text-align: left;
  }

  .launch-card {
    position: relative;
    padding: 1.75rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 10px;
    background: var(--color-surface);
  }

  .launch-card.highlighted {
    border-color: rgba(14, 165, 233, 0.5);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-md);
  }

  .badge {
    display: inline-flex;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    padding: 0.3rem 0.6rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--color-primary-muted);
    color: var(--color-primary-hover);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .badge.muted {
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.04);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  .launch-card h2 {
    font-size: 3rem;
  }

  .launch-card p,
  .fine-print {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  .launch-card ul {
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
    list-style: none;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.55rem;
  }

  .launch-card li {
    color: var(--color-text);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .launch-card li::before {
    content: '✓ ';
    color: var(--color-success);
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .card-cta {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    width: 100%;
    justify-content: center;
  }

  .fine-print {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
  }

  .readiness {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 0.75fr 1.25fr;
    gap: 3rem;
  }

  .readiness-list {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .readiness-list > div,
  details {
    padding: 1.2rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    background: var(--color-surface);
  }

  .readiness-list p,
  details p {
    margin-top: 0.6rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  .faq-on-pricing {
    max-width: 760px;
  }

  .faq-on-pricing h2 {
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  details {
    margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
  }

  summary {
    font-weight: 700;
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  summary::marker {
    color: var(--color-primary);
  }

  @media (max-width: 780px) {
    .launch-grid,
    .readiness {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
